#
# For a description of the syntax of this configuration file,
# see the file kconfig-language.txt in the NuttX tools repository.
#

config LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_PROVISION_WEB
	bool "AP-mode provisioning web entry"
	default n
	depends on NET_TCP && NET_TCPBACKLOG
	---help---
		A minimal HTTP server that serves one form, accepts an SSID and a
		passphrase, and writes them to persistent storage.  Meant to be
		started by the application through
		velasight_provisioning_start() once the radio is already in
		SoftAP; it never changes the Wi-Fi role itself, so the
		application stays in control of when the network may drop.

		NET_TCPBACKLOG is required, not merely nice to have.  Without it
		NuttX reports no poll event for a pending connection on a
		listening socket (TCP_BACKLOG is the only source of POLLIN
		there), and accept() blocks with no timeout, so a listener that
		can still be stopped is impossible.  The observed symptom of
		building without it is a service that reports "listening" and
		then never answers a request.

		The provision_web command is the manual front end for bringing
		it up over the console.

		The page is plain HTTP with no authentication, which is the usual
		trade-off for a provisioning page on an access point.  Run it
		only while provisioning.

if LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_PROVISION_WEB

config VELASIGHT_PROVISION_STORE
	string "Provisioning record path"
	default "/mnt/sdnand/prov/wifi.bin"
	---help---
		Where the credential record is written.  The default is on
		SD-NAND because that is the only persistent filesystem: /mnt is
		pseudo-filesystem and /mnt/ram is a PSRAM ramdisk.  The parent
		directory is created on demand.

		Every path component must fit 8.3.  That SD-NAND is VFAT without
		long-name support (CONFIG_FAT_LFN is not set), which rejects a
		"velasight" directory or a "wifi-provision.bin" file with
		-EINVAL rather than shortening it.

		The passphrase is stored in the clear: VFAT has no permission
		model to rely on and this part has no confirmed device key.  It
		is never logged and never echoed back over HTTP, but physical
		access to the SD-NAND reveals it.

config VELASIGHT_PROVISION_PORT
	int "Provisioning HTTP port"
	default 80
	range 1 65535
	---help---
		The port used when the caller passes 0.  80 means a phone can
		open http://<board-ip>/ with no port in the URL.

endif
